Add clearState/clearCache methods to Extbase singletons.

Several Extbase singletons accumulate per-request state:

- Backend: aggregateRootObjects, deletedEntities, changedEntities,
  visitedDuringPersistence — populated during persistAll() but never
  cleared after persist.
- ConfigurationManager: configuration cache keyed by plugin name
  leaks across pages rendering the same plugin.
- CacheService: clearCacheForTables and cacheTagStack can carry
  leftover scope from requests that threw before consuming the stack.
- ValidatorResolver: baseValidatorConjunctions caches validators
  per model class indefinitely.

Add public clearState()/clearCache() methods and expand
PersistenceManager::clearState() to also reset the Backend.

